<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- COMPARE -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section id="compare">
  <h2><span class="num">10</span>Mesh (MyLife) vs Server (BestChef)</h2>
  <p class="sub">The same monorepo ships both philosophies. This table is the cheat sheet.</p>

  <table class="compare">
    <thead>
      <tr><th style="width:24%">Concern</th><th style="width:38%">MyLife · Mesh</th><th style="width:38%">BestChef · Server</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Source of truth</strong></td><td>Each user's device(s). CRDTs converge across the mesh.</td><td>Supabase Postgres. Devices hold a cache.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Identity</strong></td><td>Per-device key + workspace symmetric keys.</td><td>Supabase Auth (email, Apple, Google, anonymous).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Transport</strong></td><td>Ranked-choice ladder: LAN → Multipeer → BLE → WebRTC → encrypted relay.</td><td>HTTPS → Supabase. Realtime over WebSocket.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Threat model</strong></td><td>Server cannot read content. Privacy-first.</td><td>Public adversarial state. Server enforces ordering, abuse mitigation, moderation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Offline</strong></td><td class="yes">First-class</td><td class="partial">Cached UI works; mutations queue.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Realtime</strong></td><td class="partial">Peer-to-peer when peers are reachable.</td><td class="yes">Server fan-out, RLS-filtered.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Authoritative ordering</strong></td><td class="no">No global order.</td><td class="yes">Postgres + cron snapshots.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Public discovery</strong></td><td class="no">Not the goal.</td><td class="yes">Indexed dishes, cuisines, leaderboards.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Moderation</strong></td><td class="no">Out of scope.</td><td class="yes">Edge function + queue + decisions.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Account deletion</strong></td><td>Local wipe; mesh peers expire eventually.</td><td>Local wipe + service-role worker + storage byte purge + audit archive.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Cost shape</strong></td><td>~zero infra; storage on user devices.</td><td>Postgres + Storage + Edge usage; scales with public traffic.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>BestChef public launch posture</strong></td><td class="no">Off launch path.</td><td class="yes">Required for launch.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- RISKS -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section id="risks">
  <h2><span class="num">11</span>Production Work &amp; Open Risks</h2>
  <p class="sub">From <code>memory.md</code> + the BestChef server-launch mission control. These are the items still standing between us and a fully public launch.</p>

  <div class="callouts">
    <div class="callout danger">
      <div class="label">Launch blocker</div>
      <h5>Production Supabase project + env</h5>
      <p>Staging is wired (<code>tcikvihyjetsfkjjpljv</code>). Prod project, env vars, and EAS secrets still need setup before the public-launch build can ship.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout danger">
      <div class="label">Launch blocker</div>
      <h5>Auth dashboard providers + templates</h5>
      <p>Apple/Google OAuth credentials, magic-link templates, and the verified deep-link redirect domain need to be configured for production.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout danger">
      <div class="label">Launch blocker</div>
      <h5>service-role deletion worker</h5>
      <p><code>bc_account_deletion_jobs</code> rows need a worker that wipes owned content, deletes media bytes, and archives the encrypted audit record per the runbook.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout warn">
      <div class="label">Launch work</div>
      <h5>Public seed-content approval</h5>
      <p>Dish catalog seeds, labels, import rollback, and added-sugar schema storage need approval and migration before opening submissions to the public.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout warn">
      <div class="label">Launch work</div>
      <h5>Contribution + moderation UI</h5>
      <p>End-user contribution flow + moderator console for media/comments still need to be wired against <code>bc_moderation_queue</code> and <code>bc_product_contributions</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout warn">
      <div class="label">Launch work</div>
      <h5>Live provider credentials</h5>
      <p>OCR, vision, OFF integration, and (later) Stripe/RevenueCat need real production credentials and rate-limit headroom.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout warn">
      <div class="label">Launch work</div>
      <h5>Legal URLs &amp; release evidence</h5>
      <p>Privacy policy, terms, and account/recovery support pages need final URLs. Release-evidence packets still require legal/pilot/release-owner signatures.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="label">Observability</div>
      <h5>Rate limits + dashboards</h5>
      <p>Per-IP and per-user rate limits on RPCs; Sentry/Logflare wiring; cost dashboards; alerting on moderation queue depth.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="label">Mobile</div>
      <h5>Android release verification</h5>
      <p>Play release tracks, crash-free rate parity with iOS, and Android-specific deep-link verification still needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout ok">
      <div class="label">Resolved</div>
      <h5>Native-safe sync facade</h5>
      <p>Hermes/Automerge <code>import.meta.url</code> failure is fixed. <code>SyncEngine</code> facades let BestChef beta builds ship without bundling the CRDT.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout ok">
      <div class="label">Resolved</div>
      <h5>Beta cloud bridge live</h5>
      <p>Hosted dish catalog seeded, <code>bc_submission_aliases</code> mapping live, comments + recipe votes flowing to staging from TestFlight.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout ok">
      <div class="label">Resolved</div>
      <h5>Identity foundation</h5>
      <p>Account lifecycle SQL, settings account UI, native auth callback, local/cloud delete-account wipe, and runbook all shipped on 2026-04-26.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight" style="margin-top:24px">
    <div class="label">★ Architecture conclusions</div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The split is intentional, not accidental.</strong> Privacy-first mesh and adversarial public server have incompatible primitives. We chose the right tool per surface instead of forcing one to do both.</li>
      <li><strong>The shared monorepo is the leverage.</strong> One UI system, one auth wrapper, one DB layer, one set of skills/agents. BestChef ships a focused Expo app on top, MyLife ships a 39-module hub — both reuse the same plumbing.</li>
      <li><strong>RPC-only writes are the production-grade fence.</strong> Votes and comments cannot be inserted with a raw client INSERT. <code>SECURITY DEFINER</code> functions enforce auth, rate, and content rules before a row exists.</li>
      <li><strong>Local SQLite is a feature, not a fallback.</strong> Kitchen flows are fast and offline because they don't pretend to be public. Publishing is an explicit, sanitized step.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  <span>Generated for the MyLife / BestChef team · architecture-tour.html</span>
  <span>Sources: <code>memory.md</code> · <code>docs/plans/features/recipes/bestchef-server-launch-mission-control.md</code> · <code>supabase/migrations/2026042400000{4,5,6,7}*.sql</code> · <code>modules/bestchef/src/db/schema.ts</code></span>
</footer>

</div><!-- /shell -->

